1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:09,000
A project workspace, not just a chat.

2
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Keep your draft while moving
between project views.

3
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Search code, knowledge, work
and project history together.

4
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Ask with retrieved evidence.
Open the sources behind the answer.

5
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Turn a saved task into a linked plan
and a separate execution session.

6
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Saved plan progress and live steps
are different views of the work.

7
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:03,000
Answer structured questions in place.
The decision stays with its session.

8
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:21,000
Accept a suggestion, or ignore it.
You decide what gets sent.

9
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:38,000
Delegate independent research
to scoped roles and models.

10
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:05,000
Inspect a child's real transcript.
Continue in a new session.

11
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:28,000
Explore an alternative in a fork
without interrupting the parent.

12
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:49,000
Pause at a safe boundary.
Continue the same conversation.

13
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:08,000
Ask a tool-free side question
without changing the main history.

14
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:26,000
Experimental Observer:
inspect suggestions before using them.

15
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:43,000
Explain code directly in Preview.
Keep the main conversation focused.

16
00:04:55,000 --> 00:05:04,000
Translate a document in place.
Preserve its code and structure.

17
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:23,000
Working forms, 2D and 3D
directly inside the conversation.

18
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:53,000
Submit an interaction back to Pix.
Choose the next action explicitly.

19
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:13,000
Run project commands in reusable
workspace terminals, not new chats.

20
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:35,000
Agent-owned background jobs
keep output and lifecycle explicit.

21
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:53,000
Review the chosen change scope.
Keep findings tied to the actual diff.

22
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:24,000
Hand a real finding to a fix session.
Review is not permission to publish.

23
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:43,000
Project knowledge is editable Markdown
with evidence-backed conflict checks.

24
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:33,000
Compare quotes, resolve, and recheck.
Export a browsable Wiki.

25
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:58,000
See usage by project and session,
alongside provider limits.

26
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:16,000
Quota remaining is not elapsed time
or measured daily consumption.

27
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:33,000
Compress closed work selectively.
Preserve the current objective.

28
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:56,000
Recover earlier decisions
from the original session history.

29
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:13,000
Different responsibilities can use
different models and thinking levels.

30
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:39,000
Inspect model use and replacements
before changing shared defaults.

31
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:58,000
Compare reusable skills and agents,
including their companion files.

32
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:28,000
Share approved project resources
and portable work through Registry.

33
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:48,000
Find and rewrite code by structure,
not by a fragile text substitution.

34
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:12,000
Compose tool calls in code.
Discover extra tools when needed.

35
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:33,000
Delegate tests of the real interface
with explicit observable outcomes.

36
00:12:51,000 --> 00:13:01,000
Inspect screenshots, accessibility
evidence and the actual QA report.

37
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:23,000
Let multiple models challenge an idea
through five research rounds.

38
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:52,000
Keep disagreement and synthesis.
Research does not authorize edits.

39
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:13,000
Dictate into the composer or search.
Review the text before submitting.

40
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:34,000
Voice uses the configured service.
Credentials stay off camera.

41
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:53,000
Reach a running Desktop session
through its private Telegram topic.

42
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:18,000
Authorized messages are real prompts.
Desktop remains the running host.

43
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:38,000
CI status belongs to the exact HEAD,
not an older run on the same branch.

44
00:15:56,000 --> 00:16:06,000
CI repair can commit and push.
Use an explicitly approved sandbox.

45
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:28,000
The Pix terminal UI is a workspace,
with tabs and live activity panels.

46
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:08,000
Snapshot undo restores its scope.
Chat history is not a disk backup.

47
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:33,000
Task, plan, session, diff and evidence:
one connected project workflow.

48
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:55,000
Show what actually ran.
Keep limits and blockers visible.
